-- title:
--   Local box of R ∩ n̂ R n⁻¹ at a place where n is a local unit
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $R$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $u$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ and let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume that the image of $n$ under the group homomorphism on units induced by the evaluation algebra map $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}\to\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_u$ at $u$ lies in [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R u`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45), that is, both that image and the image of $n^{-1}$ lie in [`Submodule.localBox R u`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_u$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_u$. Then the local box at $u$ of the order $R\sqcap\,$[`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele R n`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) — the intersection of $R$ with the set of elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lies in $n\,(\text{finite adelic box of }R)\,n^{-1}$ — coincides with [`Submodule.localBox R u`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40).
--
--   In classical terms: the order $R\cap n\hat{R}n^{-1}$ has the same completion as $R$ at every finite place where the component of $n$ is a unit of the local order, because completion commutes with intersection and with conjugation and conjugation by a local unit preserves $R_u$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset-graph constructions, where conditions imposed on $R$ away from the ramified place must be transferred to the edge order attached to a Hecke idele.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_localBox_meetOrder_eq_of_map_finiteAdeleEvalAt_mem_localBoxUnits.lean

